{"name":"Centre Stage","hex":"#c8c7cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"centre stage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Standard spelling of center stage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/centre_stage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Center Stage (1991 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Center Stage, also known as Actress and Yuen Ling-yuk, is a 1991 Hong Kong biographical docudrama film directed by Stanley Kwan. It follows the life and career of silent film actress Ruan Lingyu (1910–1935), portrayed by Maggie Cheung."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/Centre-Stage-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Center_Stage_(1991_film)","wikidata":"Q2944359"},{"title":"Center Stage (2000 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Center Stage is a 2000 American teen drama film directed by Nicholas Hytner about a group of young ballet dancers from various backgrounds who enroll at the fictitious American Ballet Academy in New York City. The film explores the issues and difficulties in the world of professional dance, and how each individual copes with the stresses. It also served as the film debut for actresses Zoe Saldaña and Amanda Schull. The film was released theatrically in the United States on May 12, 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Center_Stage_movie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Center_Stage_(2000_film)","wikidata":"Q2165006"},{"title":"Centre Stage (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Centre Stage is the debut studio album from British pop singer Kimberley Walsh, released on 4 February 2013 through Decca Records. The album is Walsh's first solo music release outside of British girl group Girls Aloud after working in acting, television presenting, and theatre. It consists of covers of songs from popular musical theatre and musical films, a passion which Walsh has wished to pursue since she was just three years old, as well as two brand new songs. Centre Stage also features duets with fellow performers Louise Dearman and Ronan Keating."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Centrestagekimberley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_Stage_(album)","wikidata":"Q5062306"},{"title":"Centre Stage (theater)","blocks":[{"text":"Centre Stage is a year-round, 285-seat theater in downtown Greenville, South Carolina. The theater maintains a full-time staff of seven and produces between six and eight mainstage productions each year, in addition to a wide variety of other entertainment and nightlife activities. Actors, directors and other theater artists are hired both locally and regionally on an as-needed basis. Centre Stage is a constituent member of Theatre Communications Group (TCG) and a member of the professional division of the Southeastern Theatre Conference (SETC)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Smithbarney_exterior.jpg/330px-Smithbarney_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_Stage_(theater)","wikidata":"Q5062308"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.608125},{"title":"Didcot Railway Centre - coaling stage - geograph.org.uk - 6535762","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Didcot_Railway_Centre_-_coaling_stage_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6535762.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.6671875,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org